Mars Rover Simulator:

A C++ based 2D rover simulation exploring autonomous navigation, terrain interaction, and robotics concepts.

Planned Features:

- 2D grid-based environment
- Manual rover control
- Obstacle and collision detection
- Terrain generation
- Battery management system
- Autonomous navigation using pathfinding algorithms (A*)

Built With:

- C++
- CMake

Project Goals:

This project aims to explore software concepts used in robotics and autonomous systems, including:
- Object-oriented programming
- Algorithms and data structures
- Pathfinding
- Simulation design